<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Tudor returns two weeks after her first visit. She stopped the over-the-counter diphenhydramine that night; for three nights she slept worse, and she now sleeps about four hours, waking at 2 or 3 in the morning and lying awake with thoughts of the friends she has lost. She has kept the sleep diary and the fixed rising time and has stopped napping after dinner. Her appetite is still poor; she takes the nutrition supplement once a day and has lost a further 0.3 kg. She still postpones audiences and has not played music or ridden. She has not had the wish not to wake since the first visit and has no thoughts of harming herself; she keeps her safety plan in her desk. She saw Dr. Rasmussen-Hale of geriatric psychiatry this afternoon. She came at the end of the day, as arranged, and asks again that nothing about her care leave the clinic. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About four hours, with early waking; diphenhydramine stopped; sleep diary kept</td></tr><tr><td>Appetite and weight</td><td>Poor; 52.1 kg, down 0.3 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Still postponing audiences; no music or riding</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No passive death wish since intake; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>16, down from 17; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Insomnia Severity Index</td><td>19 (moderate)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

